{%- comment -%}
  CREATE YOUR PERFUME
  ───────────────────
  A five-step builder that ends in a real cart line.

  The money comes from a real Shopify product and nothing else. Size and
  Strength are its two variant options; the scent family and the name the
  shopper types are line-item properties, because neither changes the price
  and putting them in variants would multiply the matrix for nothing.

  That is the same division the Mix-It-Into-a-Spray wizard already makes
  (app.js / overlays.liquid), and it is the reason this page cannot quote a
  total the cart then disagrees with — there is no price in the JavaScript to
  drift out of date.

  all_products returns nothing for a handle that is missing or unpublished.
  Rather than walk someone through four steps to a dead button, the builder is
  replaced by a short "not open yet" panel in that case, and the theme editor
  additionally gets a loud setup notice telling the merchant exactly what to
  create.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign cyp_product = all_products[section.settings.product_handle] -%}
{%- assign cyp_ready = false -%}
{%- if cyp_product.handle != blank and cyp_product.available -%}
  {%- assign cyp_ready = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

<!-- HERO -->
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">chevron_right</span><span>{{ section.settings.hero_crumb | default: 'Create Your Perfume' }}</span></div>
    <span class="ph-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.hero_eyebrow }}</span>
    <h1 class="ph-title">{{ section.settings.hero_heading }}</h1>
    <p class="ph-sub">{{ section.settings.hero_sub }}</p>
    <div class="ph-meta">
      <span><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">timer</span>{{ section.settings.meta_1 }}</span>
      <span><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">science</span>{{ section.settings.meta_2 }}</span>
      <span><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">draw</span>{{ section.settings.meta_3 }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- BUILDER -->
<section class="cyp" id="cypBuilder">
  <div class="cyp-inner">

    {%- if cyp_ready -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Everything the builder needs, written by Liquid and read by app.js.

        Variant options are emitted as a named list rather than assumed to be
        option1 = Size and option2 = Strength. A merchant who creates the
        product with the two options the other way round would otherwise get a
        builder that silently matches nothing and a Continue button that never
        enables — a support ticket with no visible cause. Resolving by name
        costs four lines and removes that entirely.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <script type="application/json" id="cypConfig">
        {
          "handle": {{ cyp_product.handle | json }},
          "title": {{ cyp_product.title | json }},
          "optionNames": [{%- for o in cyp_product.options -%}{{ o | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}],
          "variants": [
            {%- for v in cyp_product.variants -%}
            {
              "id": {{ v.id }},
              "options": [{%- for ov in v.options -%}{{ ov | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}],
              "price": {{ v.price }},
              "available": {{ v.available }}
            }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ],
          {%- comment -%}
            The separator is written before each entry except the first, not
            after each except the last. forloop.last is useless here: this loop
            runs over every block on the section, and the how-it-works and FAQ
            blocks sort after the families — so the last family is never the
            last iteration, and `unless forloop.last` would leave a trailing
            comma that makes this whole script tag invalid JSON. The builder
            would then fail to parse its config and render nothing at all.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          "families": [
            {%- assign fam_first = true -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.type == 'family' -%}
                {%- unless fam_first -%},{%- endunless -%}
                {
                  "label": {{ block.settings.label | json }},
                  "notes": {{ block.settings.notes | json }},
                  "tint": {{ block.settings.tint | default: '#C9A84C' | json }},
                  "url": {{ block.settings.url | json }}
                }
                {%- assign fam_first = false -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          ],
          "designMode": {{ request.design_mode | json }},
          "nameMax": {{ section.settings.name_max | default: 18 }},
          "namePlaceholder": {{ section.settings.name_placeholder | json }},
          "nameHelp": {{ section.settings.name_help | json }},
          "leadTime": {{ section.settings.lead_time | json }},
          "brandLine": {{ section.settings.brand_line | json }}
        }
      </script>

      <div class="cyp-grid">

        <!-- LIVE PREVIEW -->
        {%- comment -%}
          The bottle is drawn in CSS, not shipped as artwork. Two reasons: it
          has to re-tint and re-letter on every keystroke, which an image
          cannot do without a sprite per family; and it means the page has no
          asset dependency, so the feature cannot half-render because someone
          removed a file from assets/.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="cyp-preview-col">
          <div class="cyp-preview" id="cypPreview">
            <div class="cyp-bottle">
              <span class="cyp-cap"></span>
              <span class="cyp-collar"></span>
              <div class="cyp-body">
                <span class="cyp-shine" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <div class="cyp-label">
                  <span class="cyp-label-brand" id="cypBrand">{{ section.settings.brand_line }}</span>
                  <span class="cyp-label-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="cyp-label-name" id="cypBottleName">{{ section.settings.name_placeholder }}</span>
                  <span class="cyp-label-meta" id="cypBottleMeta">Your blend</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="cyp-preview-note" id="cypPreviewNote">Your bottle updates as you choose.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- STEPS -->
        <div class="cyp-steps-col">
          <div class="cyp-rail" id="cypRail" role="list"></div>
          {%- comment -%}
            A real form rather than a div, so the state app.js keeps is always
            mirrored in inputs that would actually post. app.js intercepts the
            submit and goes through the cart drawer; the inputs exist so the
            posted line and the reviewed summary cannot describe two different
            things.

            The steps themselves are rendered by JavaScript, so this form has
            nothing to collect without it — which is what the <noscript> block
            below is for. Do not describe this one as a no-JS fallback; it
            isn't, and the fallback is a separate, sibling form because
            nesting forms is invalid and the browser drops the inner one.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <form action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" method="post" id="cypForm" class="cyp-form" novalidate>
            <input type="hidden" name="id" id="cypVariantId" value="">
            <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
            <input type="hidden" name="properties[Scent family]" id="cypPropFamily" value="">
            <input type="hidden" name="properties[Bottle name]" id="cypPropName" value="">
            <div id="cypStepArea" aria-live="polite"></div>
          </form>

          {%- comment -%}
            Without JavaScript the five-step builder cannot run, but the
            product can still be bought: every sellable variant is listed flat
            with its real price, and the family and name travel as the same two
            line-item properties the builder sends. Same product, same
            properties, same order for whoever blends it — just no preview.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <noscript>
            <form action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" method="post" class="cyp-ns">
              <p class="cyp-ns-note">Our step-by-step builder needs JavaScript. You can still order a custom bottle here — we will blend it exactly the same way.</p>

              <label class="cyp-ns-label" for="cypNsFamily">Scent family</label>
              <select class="cyp-ns-field" id="cypNsFamily" name="properties[Scent family]" required>
                {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                  {%- if block.type == 'family' -%}
                    <option value="{{ block.settings.label | escape }}">{{ block.settings.label }}{% if block.settings.notes != blank %} — {{ block.settings.notes }}{% endif %}</option>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>

              <label class="cyp-ns-label" for="cypNsVariant">Size &amp; strength</label>
              <select class="cyp-ns-field" id="cypNsVariant" name="id" required>
                {%- for v in cyp_product.variants -%}
                  {%- if v.available -%}
                    <option value="{{ v.id }}">{{ v.title }} — {{ v.price | money }}</option>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>

              <label class="cyp-ns-label" for="cypNsName">Name on the bottle</label>
              <input class="cyp-ns-field" id="cypNsName" type="text" name="properties[Bottle name]" maxlength="{{ section.settings.name_max | default: 18 }}" placeholder="{{ section.settings.name_placeholder | escape }}" required>

              <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
              <button type="submit" name="add" class="btn-g">Add to Cart</button>
            </form>
          </noscript>
        </div>

      </div>

    {%- else -%}

      <div class="cyp-unavailable">
        <span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">science</span>
        <h2>{{ section.settings.closed_heading }}</h2>
        <p>{{ section.settings.closed_text }}</p>
        <a class="btn-g" href="{{ section.settings.closed_url | default: '/collections/all' }}">{{ section.settings.closed_cta | default: 'Browse the collection' }}</a>
      </div>

      {%- if request.design_mode -%}
        <div class="cyp-setup">
          <b>Setup needed — shoppers are seeing the fallback panel above.</b>
          <p>This page needs a published product with the handle <code>{{ section.settings.product_handle }}</code>, two options named <b>Size</b> and <b>Strength</b>, and a variant for each combination you sell. Create it in <i>Products</i>, then price each variant — the builder reads every price from there, so you never edit the theme to change a price.</p>
          <p>To preview against something that already exists, set <i>Product handle</i> below to <code>custom-mixed-spray</code>.</p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</section>

<!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="sec-head center"><span class="label">{{ section.settings.how_eyebrow }}</span><h2 class="sec-title">{{ section.settings.how_heading }}</h2></div>
    <div class="how-grid">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- if block.type == 'how' -%}
          <div class="how-step fade-up"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">{{ block.settings.icon | default: 'check' }}</span><h3>{{ block.settings.title }}</h3><p>{{ block.settings.text }}</p></div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
{%- assign faq_count = 0 -%}
{%- for block in section.blocks -%}
  {%- if block.type == 'faq' -%}{%- assign faq_count = faq_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if faq_count > 0 -%}
<section class="section alt">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="sec-head center"><span class="label">{{ section.settings.faq_eyebrow }}</span><h2 class="sec-title">{{ section.settings.faq_heading }}</h2></div>
    <div class="cyp-faq">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- if block.type == 'faq' -%}
          <details class="cyp-faq-item"{% if forloop.first %} open{% endif %}>
            <summary>{{ block.settings.q }}<span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">expand_more</span></summary>
            <div class="cyp-faq-a">{{ block.settings.a }}</div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}

<!-- CTA -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container"><div class="cta-band">
    <span class="label" style="color:var(--gold)">{{ section.settings.cta_eyebrow }}</span>
    <h2 class="sec-title">{{ section.settings.cta_heading }}</h2>
    <p class="sec-sub">{{ section.settings.cta_text }}</p>
    <div class="cta-actions">
      <a class="btn-g" href="{{ section.settings.cta_url | default: '/pages/find-my-scent' }}"><span class="mi" aria-hidden="true">auto_awesome</span>{{ section.settings.cta_label | default: 'Find My Scent' }}</a>
      <a class="btn-o" href="/collections/all">Shop All Products</a>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Create Your Perfume",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Product" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "product_handle", "label": "Product handle", "default": "create-your-perfume", "info": "A published product whose two options are named Size and Strength. Every price the builder quotes comes from its variants." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Hero" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hero_crumb", "label": "Breadcrumb label", "default": "Create Your Perfume" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hero_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Blended To Order In The UAE" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hero_heading", "label": "Heading (H1)", "default": "Create <em>Your Perfume</em>", "info": "Wrap words in <em></em> for the gold italic accent." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "hero_sub", "label": "Intro copy", "default": "Choose the family you love, the size you carry and the strength you wear — then put your name on the bottle. We blend it to order and ship it across the UAE." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "meta_1", "label": "Fact 1", "default": "~90 Seconds" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "meta_2", "label": "Fact 2", "default": "Blended To Order" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "meta_3", "label": "Fact 3", "default": "Your Name On It" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Bottle preview" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "brand_line", "label": "Brand line on the label", "default": "The Fragrance Secrets" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "name_placeholder", "label": "Placeholder name", "default": "Your Name" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "name_max", "label": "Maximum characters on the bottle", "min": 8, "max": 40, "step": 1, "default": 18, "info": "Keep this to what you can actually fit on the label." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "name_help", "label": "Help text under the name field", "default": "Letters, numbers, spaces, &amp; and ’ only." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "lead_time", "label": "Lead-time line on the review step", "default": "Blended to order and dispatched in 3–5 working days. We’ll WhatsApp you when it ships." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "When the product is missing" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "closed_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "The perfume bar is being restocked" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "closed_text", "label": "Text", "default": "Custom blending is paused for a few days while we restock our base oils. In the meantime, every scent family below is ready to ship today." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "closed_cta", "label": "Button label", "default": "Browse the collection" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "closed_url", "label": "Button link" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "How it works" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "how_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "How It Works" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "how_heading", "label": "Heading (H2)", "default": "Four Choices, <em>One Bottle</em>" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "FAQ" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "faq_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Before You Build" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "faq_heading", "label": "Heading (H2)", "default": "Questions, <em>Answered</em>" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Closing CTA" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Not Sure Where To Start?" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_heading", "label": "Heading (H2)", "default": "Find Your <em>Family First</em>" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "cta_text", "label": "Text", "default": "Three quick questions will tell you which family suits you — then come back and build the bottle." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Find My Scent" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta_url", "label": "Button link" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "family",
      "name": "Scent family",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Family name" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "notes", "label": "Notes", "info": "Shown under the name, e.g. Bergamot · Neroli · White Musk" },
        { "type": "color", "id": "tint", "label": "Bottle tint", "default": "#C9A84C" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "url", "label": "Matching collection", "info": "Linked from the review step so a shopper can see ready-made bottles in the same family." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "how",
      "name": "How-it-works step",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "icon", "label": "Material Symbols icon name", "default": "check" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Text" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "faq",
      "name": "FAQ item",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "q", "label": "Question" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "a", "label": "Answer" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [ { "name": "Create Your Perfume" } ]
}
{% endschema %}
